{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/smoothinganddecomposition"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Time Series Forecasting, Smoothing & Kalman Filtering","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Model trends, seasonality, volatility, and dynamic state transitions using ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExponentialSmoothing"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NelderMead"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KalmanFilter"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GARCHModel"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeSeriesDecomposition"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Temporal data analysis requires separating underlying long-term trends, periodic seasonal patterns, and random innovations. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftForecast"},{"type":"text","text":" provides hardware-accelerated time-series models leveraging Apple Accelerate FFT convolution and LAPACK linear solvers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"1. Holt-Winters Exponential Smoothing & Nelder-Mead Optimization","anchor":"1-Holt-Winters-Exponential-Smoothing--Nelder-Mead-Optimization","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExponentialSmoothing"},{"type":"text","text":" models level ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"α"},{"type":"text","text":"), trend ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"β"},{"type":"text","text":"), and seasonal ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"γ"},{"type":"text","text":") components with additive or multiplicative adjustments:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Additive Formulation:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ŷ_{t+h|t} = ℓ_t + h · b_t + s_{t+h-m(k+1)}"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameters "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"α, β, γ"},{"type":"text","text":" are automatically optimized using the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nelder-Mead simplex optimizer"}]},{"type":"text","text":" minimizing Mean Squared Error (MSE):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Synthetic monthly seasonal dataset (36 observations, 3 years)","let series = (0..<36).map { t in","    let trend = 10.0 + Double(t) * 0.5","    let seasonal = sin(Double(t % 12) * 2.0 * Double.pi \/ 12.0) * 3.0","    return trend + seasonal + Double.random(in: -0.2...0.2)","}","","\/\/ 2. Configure Triple Exponential Smoothing (Holt-Winters)","let model = ExponentialSmoothing(","    trend: .additive,","    seasonal: .additive,","    seasonalPeriods: 12",")","","\/\/ 3. Fit parameters via continuous Nelder-Mead Simplex search","try model.fit(series: series)","","if let alpha = model.alpha, let beta = model.beta, let gamma = model.gamma {","    print(\"Optimized Parameters: alpha=\\(String(format: \"%.3f\", alpha)), beta=\\(String(format: \"%.3f\", beta)), gamma=\\(String(format: \"%.3f\", gamma))\")","}","","\/\/ 4. Forecast future periods","let forecast = try model.forecast(steps: 12)","print(\"12-Month Out-of-Sample Forecast: \\(forecast)\")"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"2. High-Performance 1D Kalman Filter (LAPACK `dgesv`)","anchor":"2-High-Performance-1D-Kalman-Filter-LAPACK-dgesv","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KalmanFilter"},{"type":"text","text":" estimates the hidden state vector of a linear dynamic system over time from noisy observations. The implementation uses contiguous 1D flat buffers with Apple Accelerate LAPACK "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dgesv"},{"type":"text","text":" matrix inversions:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State Prediction:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x_{k|k-1} = F_k · x_{k-1|k-1} + B_k · u_k"},{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"text","text":"\n"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Covariance Prediction:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P_{k|k-1} = F_k · P_{k-1|k-1} · F_k^T + Q_k"},{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"text","text":"\n"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kalman Gain:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K_k = P_{k|k-1} · H_k^T · (H_k · P_{k|k-1} · H_k^T + R_k)^{-1}"}]}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Configure 2D state system: [position, velocity] with 1D observation [position]","let stateDim = 2","let obsDim = 1","","\/\/ State Transition Matrix F: position += dt * velocity","let F: [Double] = [","    1.0, 1.0,  \/\/ row 0: pos = 1.0*pos + 1.0*vel","    0.0, 1.0   \/\/ row 1: vel = 0.0*pos + 1.0*vel","]","","\/\/ Observation Matrix H: we measure position","let H: [Double] = [1.0, 0.0]","","\/\/ Process Noise Q and Measurement Noise R","let Q: [Double] = [","    0.01, 0.0,","    0.0,  0.01","]","let R: [Double] = [0.1]","","\/\/ Initial State and Covariance","let x0: [Double] = [0.0, 1.0]","let P0: [Double] = [","    1.0, 0.0,","    0.0, 1.0","]","","var kf = try KalmanFilter(","    stateDim: stateDim,","    obsDim: obsDim,","    transitionMatrix: F,","    observationMatrix: H,","    processNoise: Q,","    measurementNoise: R,","    initialState: x0,","    initialCovariance: P0",")","","\/\/ 2. Track real-time noisy trajectory","let noisyMeasurements: [[Double]] = [[0.95], [2.05], [2.98], [4.12], [5.01]]","","print(\"=== Kalman Filtering Updates ===\")","for (step, z) in noisyMeasurements.enumerated() {","    try kf.predict()","    try kf.update(observation: z)","    ","    let state = kf.state","    print(\"Step \\(step + 1): Position=\\(String(format: \"%.3f\", state[0])), Velocity=\\(String(format: \"%.3f\", state[1]))\")","}"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"3. Classical Moving-Average Seasonal Decomposition","anchor":"3-Classical-Moving-Average-Seasonal-Decomposition","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate series into Trend, Seasonal, and Residual components using a centered finite-impulse-response moving-average trend filter and equal-phase seasonal averaging (classical decomposition, "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" LOESS-based STL):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let decomp = TimeSeriesDecomposition.decompose(series: series, period: 12, type: .additive)","","print(\"Extracted Trend Component count: \\(decomp.trend.compactMap { $0 }.count)\")","print(\"Seasonal Component Cycle: \\(decomp.seasonal.prefix(12))\")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/ArimaAndSarima":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/arimaandsarima","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"ARIMA & SARIMA Time Series Models","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Forecast univariate time series with trends and periodic seasonalities using Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (ARIMA), Seasonal ARIMA (SARIMA), and Automated Order Selection (AutoARIMA)."}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/KoopmanOperator":{"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KoopmanOperator","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KoopmanOperator","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Koopman Operator time-series forecasting and dynamical system modeling actor."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Uses Extended Dynamic Mode Decomposition (EDMD) to approximate non-linear dynamics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"via linear operators in lifted observable feature spaces."}],"title":"KoopmanOperator","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/koopmanoperator","role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMAParallel":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaparallel","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using parallel Swift Concurrency."}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast","role":"collection","title":"SwiftForecast","abstract":[{"text":"Time Series & Volatility Forecasting Models.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"}}}